  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance - Master Plan Update for El Dorado International Airport in Bogota, through Government of Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This $891,840 grant supported an update to the master plan for El Dorado International Airport (BOG) in Bogota in order to plan for the development of Colombia&apos;s gateway over the next 30 years. The Unidad Administrativa Especial de Aeronautica Civil, Special Administrative Unit of Civil Aeronautics, or Aerocivil, was the grantee. Aerocivil is the agency of Colombia&apos;s Ministry of Transportation that is responsible for managing and regulating the country&apos;s airports and aeronautic infrastructure, including the award and oversight of concessions for the operation and improvement of airport infrastructure. An update of BOG&apos;s master plan is Aerocivil&apos;s current highest priority.</narrative>
  </description>
